# Tests of the `clibrary` module; generated from tools/clibrary.dsl by tools/build.py. They run under
# `refined test`, where machine and system targets work in the JIT's own process.

# Tests write C strings in the last 4 KiB of machine.state (from byte 61440), which the runtime's own state never
# reaches. Expected values are glibc's (tests/test_runtime_nolibc.py compares the library with glibc on Linux).
firstScratch is operation
firstScratch purpose "The address of the tests' scratch bytes, with a text and a 0 byte written there"
firstScratch invariant none
firstScratch typeParameter none
firstScratch input text String borrowed
firstScratch output machine.Address
firstScratch outputOwnedBy none
firstScratch raises none
firstScratch effect use machine.memory
firstScratch uses memoryAccess
firstScratch memoryHeap false
firstScratch async false
firstScratch maxRecursion none
firstScratch label begin loopKind none
firstScratch label begin within none
firstScratch let scratchAt Int64 61440 immutable
firstScratch let nul Byte 0 immutable
firstScratch at begin do findState
firstScratch at begin do findScratch
firstScratch at begin do findText
firstScratch at begin do textLength
firstScratch at begin do copyIt
firstScratch at begin do findEnd
firstScratch at begin do storeEnd
firstScratch at begin return ok place

